The initial study by Roozenbeek and van der Linden (
2019
) relied on a self-selected online sample of approximately 15,000 participants in a pre-post (within) gameplay design. Although the study provided preliminary evidence that the game increases people’s ability to detect and resist a whole range of misinformation (in the form of deceptive Twitter posts), the study suffered from a number of important theoretical and methodological limitations.
